---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactLine from '../components/ContactLine.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About | Company Name Checker"
  description="Who runs Company Name Checker, where its information comes from, and how it is checked and corrected."
>
  <h1>About Company Name Checker</h1>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    A free toolkit for people starting or running a UK limited company: check whether a name is available,
    understand why a name clashes, compare ways to register, and keep track of filing deadlines.
  </p>

  <h2>Not a government service</h2>
  <p>
    Company Name Checker is independent. It is not affiliated with Companies House or any part of the UK
    government. Only Companies House can accept a company name, and it does that when you file.
  </p>

  <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
  <p>
    Company data comes from Companies House's free public data. Fees, rules, dates and prices come from
    official pages and providers' own published pages. Each one is listed with its source and last-checked
    date on <a href="/sources/">sources</a>, and every change is logged on <a href="/data-updates/">data updates</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How content is made and checked</h2>
  <p>
    Research and drafting are done with the help of AI tools. A person checks the key facts against the
    official source before they are published.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Spotted something out of date? Contact <ContactLine />.</p>
</Base>
